301
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:55,240
At the onset of the Great War, soldiers had no body or head protection.

302
00:20:56,240 --> 00:21:01,240
The effectiveness of firearms had negated the use of armor more than 200 years earlier.

303
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:07,840
But soldiers were being struck when they stuck their heads above the trenches.

304
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:15,360
Fragments from artillery shells killed more men than direct bullet hits.

305
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:25,680
Talking to a wounded soldier motivated General Adrian to attack the problem head on.

306
00:21:28,320 --> 00:21:34,080
The soldier told Adrian his life had been saved by a mess bowl he was wearing on his head at the time he was hit.

307
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:39,240
Inspired, the general ordered the manufacturing

308
00:21:39,241 --> 00:21:44,240
